  "title": "What Is Zonal OCR? How It Works, Benefits, and Best Use Cases",
  "summary": "Zonal OCR is a document processing automation that extracts text from predefined areas of a document. Unlike full-page OCR, which captures all available text and allows you to process complete documents, zonal OCR lets you define exactly which fields to read before any processing begins.",
